Below you will receive task descriptions from which you should generate an Ansible Playbook.
The generated playbook must be valid inside an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory (e.g., tasks/main.yml).
Do not include hosts:, vars:, or any playbook-level headers. Only output valid task entries or blocks as expected in a role.

Task 1: Install apache httpd
Description Task 1: The playbook should install the apache httpd package.

Task 2: Configure selinux
Description Task 2: The playbook should configure selinux, if it is enabled. It should modify the specified seboolean settings and allow connections to the custom port.

Task 3: Configure httpd
Description Task 3: The playbook should configure httpd using a template. It should notify the test httpd configuration validity and restart httpd.

Task 4: Activate httpd module | Debian
Description Task 4: The playbook should activate the httpd module using the command, if the OS family is Debian. It should notify the test httpd configuration validity.

Task 5: Import ssl.yml
Description Task 5: The playbook should import the ssl.yml file, if https_ssl_enable is true.

Task 6: Import locations.yml
Description Task 6: The playbook should import the locations.yml file, if httpd_locations is defined.

Task 7: Import vhosts.yml
Description Task 7: The playbook should import the vhosts.yml file, if httpd_vhosts is defined.

Task 8: Configure ports
Description Task 8: The playbook should configure the ports using a template, if the OS family is Debian or Suse. It should notify the test httpd configuration validity and restart httpd.

Task 9: Import directories.yml
Description Task 9: The playbook should import the directories.yml file, if httpd_directories is defined.

Task 10: Flush handlers
Description Task 10: The playbook should flush the handlers.

Task 11: Removing default html
Description Task 11: The playbook should remove the default html file, if httpd_remove_example is true.

Task 12: Start and enable httpd
Description Task 12: The playbook should start and enable the httpd service.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook: 
---
- name: Install apache httpd
  package:
    name: httpd
    state: present

- name: Configure selinux
  when: ansible_facts.selinux.is_selinux_enabled == 1
  block:
    - name: Modify selinux booleans
      seboolean:
        httpd_can_network_connect: true
        httpd_can_sendmail: true
      when: ansible_facts.selinux.is_selinux_enabled == 1

    - name: Allow connections to custom port
      seport:
        port: 8080
        protocol: tcp
        selevel: s0
        tylevel: s0
        seuser: system_u
        tsuser: system_u

- name: Configure httpd
  template:
    src: httpd.conf.j2
    dest: /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf
  notify: test httpd configuration

- name: Activate httpd module | Debian
  when: ansible_facts.os_family == "Debian"
  command: a2enmod httpd
  notify: test httpd configuration

- name: Import ssl.yml
  when: https_ssl_enable == true
  import_tasks: ssl.yml

- name: Import locations.yml
  when: httpd_locations is defined
  import_tasks: locations.yml

- name: Import vhosts.yml
  when: httpd_vhosts is defined
  import_tasks: vhosts.yml

- name: Configure ports
  when: ansible_facts.os_family in ["Debian", "Suse"]
  template:
    src: ports.conf.j2
    dest: /etc/httpd/conf/ports.conf
  notify: test httpd configuration

- name: Import directories.yml
  when: httpd_directories is defined
  import_tasks: directories.yml

- name: Flush handlers
  meta: flush_handlers

- name: Removing default html
  when: httpd_remove_example == true
  file:
    path: /var/www/html/index.html
    state: absent

- name: Start and enable httpd
  service:
    name: httpd
    state: started
    enabled: yes

